{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-58351","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68256","text":"SpecPrompt — Implementation Build Prompt"}]},{"id":"blk-58352","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68257","marks":["bold"],"text":"Version:"},{"id":"spn-68258","text":" 1.0 | "},{"id":"spn-68259","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date:"},{"id":"spn-68260","text":" April 2026 | "},{"id":"spn-68261","marks":["bold"],"text":"Type:"},{"id":"spn-68262","text":" Full Implementation (CLI + MCP + Supabase)"}]},{"id":"blk-58353","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68263","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58354","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68264","text":"Your Mission"}]},{"id":"blk-58355","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68265","text":"You are building "},{"id":"spn-68266","marks":["bold"],"text":"SpecPrompt"},{"id":"spn-68267","text":" — the standards layer of the [&] Protocol dark factory pipeline. SpecPrompt defines the SPEC.md format (machine-parseable agent specifications) and provides the CLI toolchain, MCP server, and Supabase registry that make specs the entry point for autonomous code generation."}]},{"id":"blk-58356","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68268","marks":["bold"],"text":"Read `docs/spec/README.md` fully before writing a single line."},{"id":"spn-68269","text":" It is the authoritative spec."}]},{"id":"blk-58357","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68270","text":"SpecPrompt is the "},{"id":"spn-68271","marks":["bold"],"text":"first stage"},{"id":"spn-68272","text":" of the dark factory pipeline:"}]},{"id":"blk-58358","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"SpecPrompt (spec in) → Agentelic (build) → OS-008 (enforce) → FleetPrompt (distribute) → RuneFort (observe)"},{"id":"blk-58359","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68273","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58360","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68274","text":"Target Stack"}]},{"id":"blk-58361","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Language:   Elixir 1.17+ / OTP 27\nCLI:        Mix escript (specprompt validate, lint, test-gen, test-compile, diff, publish)\nMCP:        JSON-RPC over HTTP (spec_validate, spec_lint, spec_generate, spec_test_gen,\n            spec_test_compile, spec_test_approve, spec_diff, spec_search)\nDatabase:   PostgreSQL via shared Supabase (spec.* schema, migration range TBD)\nAuth:       Supabase Auth (shared [&] ecosystem — amp.profiles, amp.workspaces)\nParser:     PEG grammar (see spec section 4.4) — implement in both Elixir and TypeScript\nTesting:    ExUnit (Elixir), Vitest (TypeScript parser)\nDeploy:     Fly.io (MCP server) + npm (TypeScript parser)"},{"id":"blk-58362","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68275","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58363","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68276","text":"Dual-Mode Architecture"}]},{"id":"blk-58364","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68277","text":"SpecPrompt operates in two modes. Both must work from day one:"}]},{"id":"blk-58365","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68278","text":"Filesystem Mode (default, zero-cost)"}]},{"id":"blk-58366","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58368","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68279","text":"CLI reads "},{"id":"spn-68280","marks":["code"],"text":".md"},{"id":"spn-68281","text":" files from local git repos"}]}],"id":"blk-58367","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58370","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68282","text":"No auth, no database, no network"}]}],"id":"blk-58369","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58372","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68283","text":"All tools work offline: validate, lint, test-gen, test-compile, diff"}]}],"id":"blk-58371","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58374","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68284","text":"Audit via git history"}]}],"id":"blk-58373","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58376","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68285","text":"This is the \"PULSE scales down\" demonstration"}]}],"id":"blk-58375","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58377","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68286","text":"Registry Mode (multi-tenant dark factory)"}]},{"id":"blk-58378","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58380","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68287","text":"Specs stored in Supabase "},{"id":"spn-68288","marks":["code"],"text":"spec.specs"},{"id":"spn-68289","text":" table"}]}],"id":"blk-58379","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58382","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68290","text":"Workspace-scoped via "},{"id":"spn-68291","marks":["code"],"text":"amp.workspaces"}]}],"id":"blk-58381","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58384","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68292","text":"Auth via Supabase Auth (same identity as all [&] products)"}]}],"id":"blk-58383","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58386","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68293","text":"Visibility: private | workspace | public"}]}],"id":"blk-58385","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58388","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68294","text":"Pipeline triggers via Supabase Realtime or CloudEvents webhooks"}]}],"id":"blk-58387","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58390","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68295","text":"Required for dark factory automation"}]}],"id":"blk-58389","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58391","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68296","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58392","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68297","text":"Repository Structure"}]},{"id":"blk-58393","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68298","text":"Create this structure inside "},{"id":"spn-68299","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt.com/"},{"id":"spn-68300","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-58394","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"specprompt.com/\n├── lib/\n│   ├── specprompt/\n│   │   ├── parser.ex              # PEG-based SPEC.md parser (section 4.3-4.4)\n│   │   ├── spec.ex                # SpecPrompt.Spec Ecto schema (section 4.6)\n│   │   ├── capability.ex          # SpecPrompt.Capability embedded schema\n│   │   ├── constraint.ex          # SpecPrompt.Constraint embedded schema\n│   │   ├── acceptance_test.ex     # SpecPrompt.AcceptanceTest embedded schema\n│   │   ├── compiled_test.ex       # SpecPrompt.CompiledTest embedded schema (NEW)\n│   │   ├── dependency.ex          # SpecPrompt.Dependency embedded schema\n│   │   ├── changelog_entry.ex     # SpecPrompt.ChangelogEntry embedded schema\n│   │   ├── validator.ex           # Validation rules (section 4.7 — all MUST + SHOULD rules)\n│   │   ├── linter.ex              # Best-practice linting\n│   │   ├── differ.ex              # Spec version diffing\n│   │   ├── test_generator.ex      # Generate test scaffolding from acceptance tests\n│   │   ├── test_compiler.ex       # Compile natural language tests → Agentelic DSL assertions (NEW)\n│   │   ├── publisher.ex           # Publish to FleetPrompt registry or Supabase\n│   │   ├── registry.ex            # Supabase registry client (spec.specs CRUD)\n│   │   ├── interop/\n│   │   │   ├── ampersand.ex       # Bidirectional ampersand.json mapping (section 4.8)\n│   │   │   └── adl.ex             # Bidirectional ADL mapping (section 4.8)\n│   │   └── mcp/\n│   │       ├── server.ex          # MCP JSON-RPC server (section 4.2)\n│   │       └── tools.ex           # Tool definitions and handlers\n│   ├── specprompt.ex              # Application entry point\n│   └── cli.ex                     # CLI escript entry point\n├── test/\n│   ├── parser_test.exs\n│   ├── validator_test.exs\n│   ├── linter_test.exs\n│   ├── test_compiler_test.exs\n│   ├── differ_test.exs\n│   └── fixtures/\n│       ├── valid_spec.md          # Use the customer-support example from spec section 3.3\n│       ├── invalid_spec.md        # Missing required sections\n│       └── compiled_tests.json    # Pre-compiled test assertions\n├── npm/                           # TypeScript parser package (@specprompt/parser)\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── parser.ts\n│   │   ├── types.ts\n│   │   └── index.ts\n│   ├── test/\n│   │   └── parser.test.ts\n│   ├── package.json\n│   └── tsconfig.json\n├── mix.exs\n├── Dockerfile\n└── fly.toml"},{"id":"blk-58395","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68301","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58396","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68302","text":"Implementation Order"}]},{"id":"blk-58397","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68303","text":"Phase 1: Parser + Validator (week 1)"}]},{"id":"blk-58398","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68304","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-68305","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement PEG parser"},{"id":"spn-68306","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-68307","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/parser.ex"},{"id":"spn-68308","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-58399","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58401","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68309","text":"Parse YAML frontmatter (all fields from spec section 4.5, including new "},{"id":"spn-68310","marks":["code"],"text":"workspace_id"},{"id":"spn-68311","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68312","marks":["code"],"text":"visibility"},{"id":"spn-68313","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68314","marks":["code"],"text":"source_hash"},{"id":"spn-68315","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-58400","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58403","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68316","text":"Parse H2 sections: Purpose, Capabilities, Constraints, Acceptance Tests, Architecture, Dependencies, Changelog"}]}],"id":"blk-58402","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58405","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68317","text":"Extract structured data into "},{"id":"spn-68318","marks":["code"],"text":"SpecPrompt.Spec"},{"id":"spn-68319","text":" schema"}]}],"id":"blk-58404","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58407","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68320","text":"Compute "},{"id":"spn-68321","marks":["code"],"text":"source_hash"},{"id":"spn-68322","text":" (SHA-256 of raw SPEC.md content)"}]}],"id":"blk-58406","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58409","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68323","text":"Return "},{"id":"spn-68324","marks":["code"],"text":"{:ok, %SpecPrompt.Spec{}}"},{"id":"spn-68325","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-68326","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, [errors]}"}]}],"id":"blk-58408","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58410","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68327","text":"2. "},{"id":"spn-68328","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement validator"},{"id":"spn-68329","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-68330","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/validator.ex"},{"id":"spn-68331","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-58411","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58413","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68332","text":"All 8 MUST rules from spec section 4.7"}]}],"id":"blk-58412","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58415","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68333","text":"All 7 SHOULD warnings (including 3 new compiled test warnings)"}]}],"id":"blk-58414","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58417","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68334","text":"Return structured validation result with line numbers"}]}],"id":"blk-58416","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58418","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68335","text":"3. "},{"id":"spn-68336","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement CLI"},{"id":"spn-68337","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-68338","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/cli.ex"},{"id":"spn-68339","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-58419","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58421","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68340","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt validate SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-68341","text":" — parse + validate, exit 0/1"}]}],"id":"blk-58420","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58423","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68342","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt lint SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-68343","text":" — validate + SHOULD warnings"}]}],"id":"blk-58422","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58424","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68344","text":"4. "},{"id":"spn-68345","marks":["bold"],"text":"Write tests"},{"id":"spn-68346","text":" against the customer-support example from spec section 3.3"}]},{"id":"blk-58425","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68347","text":"Phase 2: Test Compilation (week 2)"}]},{"id":"blk-58426","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68348","text":"This is the critical dark factory bridge — turning natural language acceptance tests into executable assertions."}]},{"id":"blk-58427","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68349","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-68350","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement test compiler"},{"id":"spn-68351","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-68352","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/test_compiler.ex"},{"id":"spn-68353","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-58428","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58430","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68354","text":"Input: "},{"id":"spn-68355","marks":["code"],"text":"%SpecPrompt.Spec{}"},{"id":"spn-68356","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-68357","marks":["code"],"text":"acceptance_tests"}]}],"id":"blk-58429","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58432","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68358","text":"For each acceptance test, generate a "},{"id":"spn-68359","marks":["code"],"text":"%SpecPrompt.CompiledTest{}"},{"id":"spn-68360","text":":"}]}],"id":"blk-58431","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58434","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68361","marks":["code"],"text":"setup"},{"id":"spn-68362","text":": mocked tool states derived from the "},{"id":"spn-68363","marks":["code"],"text":"given"},{"id":"spn-68364","text":" clause"}]}],"id":"blk-58433","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58436","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68365","marks":["code"],"text":"input"},{"id":"spn-68366","text":": agent input derived from the "},{"id":"spn-68367","marks":["code"],"text":"given"},{"id":"spn-68368","text":" clause"}]}],"id":"blk-58435","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58438","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68369","marks":["code"],"text":"assertions"},{"id":"spn-68370","text":": list of Agentelic DSL assertions:"}]}],"id":"blk-58437","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58440","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68371","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :contains, value: \"...\"}"},{"id":"spn-68372","text":" — expected text in output"}]}],"id":"blk-58439","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58442","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68373","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :tool_called, tool: \"...\", args: %{}}"},{"id":"spn-68374","text":" — expected tool invocation"}]}],"id":"blk-58441","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58444","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68375","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :tool_not_called, tool: \"...\"}"},{"id":"spn-68376","text":" — forbidden tool invocation"}]}],"id":"blk-58443","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58446","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68377","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :escalated, value: true/false}"},{"id":"spn-68378","text":" — escalation check"}]}],"id":"blk-58445","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58448","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68379","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :constraint_respected, constraint_index: N}"},{"id":"spn-68380","text":" — constraint enforcement"}]}],"id":"blk-58447","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58450","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68381","text":"Compilation is "},{"id":"spn-68382","marks":["bold"],"text":"LLM-assisted on first pass"},{"id":"spn-68383","text":": send the spec + acceptance test to an LLM, ask it to generate the assertion mapping"}]}],"id":"blk-58449","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58452","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68384","text":"Cache compiled tests by "},{"id":"spn-68385","marks":["code"],"text":"{source_hash, test_index}"},{"id":"spn-68386","text":" — unchanged tests reuse prior compilations"}]}],"id":"blk-58451","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58454","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68387","text":"Mark all compiled tests as "},{"id":"spn-68388","marks":["code"],"text":"approved: false"},{"id":"spn-68389","text":" initially"}]}],"id":"blk-58453","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58455","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68390","text":"2. "},{"id":"spn-68391","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement approval workflow"}]},{"id":"blk-58456","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58458","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68392","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --output tests/compiled.json"},{"id":"spn-68393","text":" — compile all tests"}]}],"id":"blk-58457","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58460","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68394","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --approve"},{"id":"spn-68395","text":" — mark all compiled tests as approved"}]}],"id":"blk-58459","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58462","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68396","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --status"},{"id":"spn-68397","text":" — show compilation + approval status"}]}],"id":"blk-58461","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58464","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68398","text":"Only approved tests are used by Agentelic in the dark factory pipeline"}]}],"id":"blk-58463","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58465","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68399","text":"3. "},{"id":"spn-68400","marks":["bold"],"text":"Important constraint"},{"id":"spn-68401","text":": The test compiler itself does NOT call LLMs. It generates a structured prompt that an external LLM (via Agentelic or the user's own API key) processes. SpecPrompt is a tool, not an agent. The MCP server version ("},{"id":"spn-68402","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_test_compile"},{"id":"spn-68403","text":") returns the prompt for the agent t